  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia Flood Joint Response 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To respond to outbreaks of Acute Watery Diarrhea/Cholera as well as damaged health facilities due to flooding, WV/SRDA will provide an integrated multisectoral response in Health and WASH with Protection mainstreamed, targeting 44,181 flood affected individuals in Jowhar.To address the urgent need for clean water, WV will do immediate water trucking to 600 HHs, while working on rehabilitation of 4 emergency water kiosks and 1 shallow well. To prevent waterborne diseases, hygiene promotion sessions will be held targeting 6000 individuals. 200 vulnerable flood-affected HHs will receive WASH NFI kits including soap, aqua tabs and 2 jerrycans. Menstrual Hygiene Management (MHM) will be provided to 200 women/girls.Lifesaving primary health care services will be upscaled targeting 44,181 individuals, including medicine and supply provision; disease surveillance, outbreak support to health facilities and strengthened referral mechanisms. 1 health facility will be renovated after flooding damage. To control vector borne diseases, mosquito nets will be provided.Protection mainstreaming will be undertaken by integrating protection and GBV messages in health and wash activities, training of relevant staff and volunteers on PSEA, PFA and GBV, and referral service to SGBV victims within 72 hours.WV/SDRA&#x2019;s coordination efforts are comprehensive, as we actively participate in the El Nino coordination mechanisms at both the federal level (SoDMA) and state level (MOHADMA), with following outlined protocols. WV/SDRA is well-informed and actively participating in the implementation of the project with the acquired support. The project will additionally collaborate with key entities, including local authorities, communities, Somalia Water and Land Information Management (SWALIM), Ministry of Health, DRA Partners and the Inter-Cluster Coordination Group under OCHA. This collaborative approach will ensure relevant standards are followed and efforts are not duplicated.</narrative>
  </description>
